<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maragha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maragha is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>. It served as an early capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a>. Hulagu founded a famous astronomical observatory there, directed by the scholar Nasir al-Din al-Tusi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maragha.jpg" alt="Maragha" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maragheh State University · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maraghe.city.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
